 "_doc": "Task 52: how the world reacts when the player does something that does not fit (SocialFit.gap: how far the act is from what the two people have between them). Below min_gap the normal scored outcome runs. Above it the act still works with the probability (1 - gap)^success_pow (a close fit often works), otherwise one reaction is drawn from the act's group by weight. A weight is multiplied by: the target's traits (traits), their mood (moods), the kind of place (places), whether the target has a partner (partner), and gap_scale (up = more likely the further out of place, down = less likely). Effects: fr / ro / tr / te = friendship, romance, trust, tension of the target towards the player; abuf / tbuf = buff on the player's person / on the other; witness = reputation lost with onlookers (and gossip); act = a special consequence (report = they go to the police with a harassment complaint); tier = how the result reads (good, meh, bad). lines: what the other person says or does ({t} = them, {a} = the player's person); a line is never used twice in a row for the same pair (PlayerPrompt._pick). Groups: touch (kiss, cuddle, hold hands, sneak kiss, slow dance), romance (flirt, wink, sweet nothings, ask out, confess, make official), deep (secrets, advice, dreams, confiding), mean (insults, rumours, blame, mock, yell), funny (pranks, tickling, teasing, roasts), friendly (hugs, hangouts, high fives).",
